Because even if you want to
stream all the time, every day,

01:04:21.120 --> 01:04:24.063
to see chat, to make them happy, etcetera.

01:04:24.063 --> 01:04:25.074
At the end at the end of the day,

01:04:25.074 --> 01:04:28.141
I only have so much energy and
chat's not going to have fun,

01:04:28.141 --> 01:04:29.820
'cause they can tell when I'm low energy.

01:04:29.820 --> 01:04:31.096
Like I said, I've seen
paragraphs analyzing

01:04:31.096 --> 01:04:32.399
every single facet of my personality.

01:04:32.399 --> 01:04:35.454
They can tell when you're
low energy, that's the truth.

01:04:35.454 --> 01:04:37.554
So sometimes it's worth
it to give yourself

01:04:37.554 --> 01:04:39.016
a little more breathing room.

01:04:39.016 --> 01:04:41.315
Occasionally though, I get
a little ahead of myself,

01:04:41.315 --> 01:04:43.795
schedule too many
streams, it be like that.

01:04:43.795 --> 01:04:45.257
And it's taking quite a toll on my energy,

01:04:45.257 --> 01:04:47.718
and after I'm done streaming,
I just go lay down.

01:04:47.718 --> 01:04:49.630
And that's the only thing
I do besides streaming

01:04:49.630 --> 01:04:51.175
and making music, is sleeping.

01:04:51.175 --> 01:04:52.873
So it's something that I-

01:04:52.873 --> 01:04:53.802
- How much sleep do you get per day?

01:04:53.802 --> 01:04:56.182
- Six hours a night,
which is not terrible,

01:04:56.182 --> 01:04:57.964
but it's not perfect.

01:04:57.964 --> 01:04:58.797
- I think you need a
little bit more than that.

01:04:58.797 --> 01:05:02.544
- Yeah, so I'm trying to
work on that a little bit,

01:05:02.544 --> 01:05:03.722
but there's just a lot to do.

01:05:03.722 --> 01:05:06.322
And there's a lot that you
have to put your energy into.

01:05:06.322 --> 01:05:09.127
And when it comes to music,
one thing that I've noticed

01:05:09.127 --> 01:05:11.321
is that it takes a little less energy

01:05:11.321 --> 01:05:13.515
for me simply because there's no pressure

01:05:13.515 --> 01:05:15.274
about making mistakes on stream.

01:05:15.274 --> 01:05:17.161
In your work process,

01:05:17.161 --> 01:05:19.599
nobody really sees all the awful mistakes

01:05:19.599 --> 01:05:21.334
that you make when you're
recording a hundred takes

01:05:21.334 --> 01:05:22.443
over and over again.

01:05:22.443 --> 01:05:24.396
You put it together and
the song that you've made

01:05:24.396 --> 01:05:26.038
is hopefully, if you've done it right,

01:05:26.038 --> 01:05:27.163
the best possible thing

01:05:27.163 --> 01:05:29.281
that you could have made it be, right.

01:05:29.281 --> 01:05:31.900
With streaming, it's just
go, be good at improv,

01:05:31.900 --> 01:05:34.251
be good at games, be good
at something and just pray.

01:05:34.251 --> 01:05:35.151
- Be perfect for the next two hours.

01:05:35.151 --> 01:05:36.869
- Yeah, exactly and just pray.

01:05:36.869 --> 01:05:38.652
And that takes a lot of energy out of you.

01:05:38.652 --> 01:05:41.107
there's a lot of stress
that comes with that.

01:05:41.107 --> 01:05:43.928
That maybe you can be
really good at hiding,

01:05:43.928 --> 01:05:45.710
maybe you're not so good at hiding it.

01:05:45.710 --> 01:05:47.911
It just depends, man and it's rough.

01:05:47.911 --> 01:05:49.425
It's-

01:05:49.425 --> 01:05:50.258
- I feel like you've got to learn it along

01:05:50.258 --> 01:05:52.868
the way as well because no
one's ever prepared to be like,

01:05:52.868 --> 01:05:55.288
"Okay, I'm going to stream
even though I'm low energy."

01:05:55.288 --> 01:05:58.945
And sometimes you have to
just force it out of you,

01:05:58.945 --> 01:06:00.124
and it's so difficult

01:06:00.124 --> 01:06:02.570
'cause that's why I don't
stream so often as well,

01:06:02.570 --> 01:06:03.610
because I also have a
certain amount of energy,

01:06:03.610 --> 01:06:05.150
and if it's below that,

01:06:05.150 --> 01:06:08.749
then it's just not going
to be a good stream.

01:06:08.749 --> 01:06:11.029
- I think that a lot of the times though,

01:06:11.029 --> 01:06:13.532
when you feel rough or you
don't feel like you've got

01:06:13.532 --> 01:06:14.844
the energy for a stream,

01:06:14.844 --> 01:06:17.346
often, that when you actually
start and get into it,

01:06:17.346 --> 01:06:18.908
you kind of get into the rhythm of it,

01:06:18.908 --> 01:06:21.328
and you kind of get a lot
more energy as you go.

01:06:21.328 --> 01:06:22.161
- It also depends on what you're doing.

01:06:22.161 --> 01:06:23.970
There are some streams
where you're just like,

01:06:23.970 --> 01:06:25.848
"I'm having a good time playing this",

01:06:25.848 --> 01:06:27.154
or "I'm having a good
time doing this activity."

01:06:27.154 --> 01:06:29.293
And there some streams
where you're just like,

01:06:29.293 --> 01:06:30.837
"This isn't an okay time and I'll have

01:06:30.837 --> 01:06:32.619
to make it seem like it's a lot more fun

01:06:32.619 --> 01:06:33.977
than just an okay time."

01:06:33.977 --> 01:06:35.580
- I mean, I do got to admit,

01:06:35.580 --> 01:06:39.057
I think I barely scraped by
in terms of the personality

01:06:39.057 --> 01:06:41.797
you need to stream because
not everyone can stream.

01:06:41.797 --> 01:06:43.933
You have to have a certain
kind of personality.

01:06:43.933 --> 01:06:45.158
I don't know if you guys know this,

01:06:45.158 --> 01:06:48.600
but I've seen it a couple
quote, unquote, reliable,

01:06:48.600 --> 01:06:51.218
scientific research papers or whatever.

01:06:51.218 --> 01:06:52.496
Somebody said something on the internet,

01:06:52.496 --> 01:06:53.655
and I took it as fact.

01:06:53.655 --> 01:06:54.556
But I believe it.

01:06:54.556 --> 01:06:55.389
I can only-

01:06:55.389 --> 01:06:56.222
(Garnt laughs)

01:06:56.222 --> 01:06:58.324
- There's some big air quotations on that.

01:06:58.324 --> 01:06:59.957
- I can understand this being true,

01:06:59.957 --> 01:07:01.842
so I'm not saying this is a fact,

01:07:01.842 --> 01:07:05.842
but I don't think the
human brain was meant

01:07:05.842 --> 01:07:10.613
to deal with 10,000 or so
people watching you all

01:07:10.613 --> 01:07:11.797
at one time and what you're doing.

01:07:11.797 --> 01:07:12.778
- 100%.
- 100%..

01:07:12.778 --> 01:07:14.512
- Humans weren't built to do that.

01:07:14.512 --> 01:07:16.702
- 100%.
- 100%.

01:07:16.702 --> 01:07:17.741
- We weren't built for it.

01:07:17.741 --> 01:07:19.854
Now, technically I'm
not a human but listen.

01:07:19.854 --> 01:07:20.876
(Garnt and Connor laughs)

01:07:20.876 --> 01:07:22.890
I have a human body, so we're going-

01:07:22.890 --> 01:07:25.302
- Throw out the research paper.

01:07:25.302 --> 01:07:26.228
(Connor chuckles)

01:07:26.228 --> 01:07:27.061
(Garnt and Mori laughs)
- Exactly.

01:07:27.061 --> 01:07:27.894
But we really aren't meant to,

01:07:27.894 --> 01:07:30.634
so you have to have a
certain kind of personality

01:07:30.634 --> 01:07:31.823
to not mentally collapse.

01:07:31.823 --> 01:07:32.845
- What is that personality?

01:07:32.845 --> 01:07:35.487
- You have to have a little bit of an ego.

01:07:35.487 --> 01:07:37.153
You have to have just a smidge.

01:07:37.153 --> 01:07:40.072
It just needs to be a little
bit, it needs to be enough.

01:07:40.072 --> 01:07:43.075
Because not everyone can do
it, that's just the truth.

01:07:43.075 --> 01:07:44.693
You have to have a certain
kind of personality,

01:07:44.693 --> 01:07:46.291
you can't brute force it and that's fine.

01:07:46.291 --> 01:07:49.894
That is absolutely okay but
it's just kind of how it is.

01:07:49.894 --> 01:07:52.518
You can build it up yourself
but it is a prerequisite.

01:07:52.518 --> 01:07:54.457
- Do you see yourself doing streaming

01:07:54.457 --> 01:07:56.297
for a much longer time?

01:07:56.297 --> 01:07:58.386
Or do you think there's like
a certain amount of time?

01:07:58.386 --> 01:07:59.927
Where you're just like,
"Yeah, I'm probably going

01:07:59.927 --> 01:08:01.349
to try something different
after a certain amount of time."

01:08:01.349 --> 01:08:03.648
- Right, like a time limit on this?

01:08:03.648 --> 01:08:05.427
It does take more energy for me

01:08:05.427 --> 01:08:06.806
than some other folks, I think.

01:08:06.806 --> 01:08:08.382
And with that being said,

01:08:08.382 --> 01:08:10.521
I think that I'd like to try it out,

01:08:10.521 --> 01:08:12.081
and continue on for a longer time.

01:08:12.081 --> 01:08:14.428
However, the frequency with
which I do it may change

01:08:14.428 --> 01:08:16.082
at some point because-

01:08:16.082 --> 01:08:17.284
- Yeah I mean-

01:08:17.284 --> 01:08:18.441
- Yeah, I'll be thoroughly impressed

01:08:18.441 --> 01:08:19.676
if you can keep this for the next year.

01:08:19.676 --> 01:08:24.331
- Have you heard about this
thing, it's called weekends.

01:08:24.331 --> 01:08:25.793
It's where most people-

01:08:25.793 --> 01:08:27.004
- A holiday.

01:08:27.004 --> 01:08:28.069
- Holidays as well.

01:08:28.069 --> 01:08:29.108
(Garnt laughs)

01:08:29.108 --> 01:08:30.745
- The fabled holiday,
I've heard of that before.

01:08:30.745 --> 01:08:33.641
Yeah, but in a sense, these days,

01:08:33.641 --> 01:08:34.866
I kind of find myself sitting down

01:08:34.866 --> 01:08:36.542
after a stream being like,
"All right, break time,

01:08:36.542 --> 01:08:37.563
watch something on Netflix."

01:08:37.563 --> 01:08:39.496
And I think to myself,

01:08:39.496 --> 01:08:42.641
"I want to do something work-related."

01:08:42.641 --> 01:08:44.465
And that's when you've become a workaholic

01:08:44.465 --> 01:08:46.404
and you need to fix that.
- You've got the illness.

01:08:46.404 --> 01:08:49.337
- So it's good but I
often found the struggle

01:08:49.337 --> 01:08:54.223
where I would sometimes
invest too heavily in work.

01:08:54.223 --> 01:08:57.283
And then I would think,
"Oh, I just haven't hung out

01:08:57.283 --> 01:08:58.381
with anyone in a long time."

01:08:58.381 --> 01:08:59.442
(Joey chuckles)

01:08:59.442 --> 01:09:00.481
And I feel kind of lonely.

01:09:00.481 --> 01:09:03.424
But then I've spent too much time working

01:09:03.424 --> 01:09:05.183
and I can't hang out with people

01:09:05.183 --> 01:09:06.621
because they're hanging out with people

01:09:06.621 --> 01:09:07.784
who are more consistent
(laughing) hanging out,

01:09:07.784 --> 01:09:09.346
which is totally fair, right.

01:09:09.346 --> 01:09:10.466
- What do you mean?

01:09:10.466 --> 01:09:12.207
Well, because if you're
often not available,

01:09:12.207 --> 01:09:13.529
people don't invite you to things, right?

01:09:13.529 --> 01:09:16.025
So if everyone knows that
you're not going to turn up

01:09:16.025 --> 01:09:18.324
to stuff most of the time,
people stop inviting you.

01:09:18.324 --> 01:09:19.345
- They give up.

01:09:19.345 --> 01:09:20.773
- So you kind of have to
balance very carefully

01:09:20.773 --> 01:09:22.097
and like, going to stuff,

01:09:22.097 --> 01:09:24.178
but also wanting to be there for work.

01:09:24.178 --> 01:09:25.684
Because I also feel the
same way with streaming

01:09:25.684 --> 01:09:27.721
where I'm like, "Oh, I'm not there enough.

01:09:27.721 --> 01:09:31.309
I'm not participating in
the ecosystem enough."

01:09:31.309 --> 01:09:32.324
So it's a struggle.

01:09:32.324 --> 01:09:33.584
Do you ever have that problem?

01:09:33.584 --> 01:09:35.043
- All the time.

01:09:35.043 --> 01:09:35.876
(Connor chuckles)

01:09:35.876 --> 01:09:38.693
But I mean, recently I've
been trying to fix that

01:09:38.693 --> 01:09:41.630
by instead reaching out to
people that I haven't talked to,

01:09:41.630 --> 01:09:42.814
and be like, hey I'm here.

01:09:42.814 --> 01:09:43.911
- That's yeah, that's my work around.

01:09:43.911 --> 01:09:47.045
It's because people, if I get to the point

01:09:47.045 --> 01:09:49.147
where people stop inviting
me because I get too busy,

01:09:49.147 --> 01:09:50.218
get your brain.

01:09:50.218 --> 01:09:51.120
I stopped.
- No, no, I do,

01:09:51.120 --> 01:09:51.953
I have to have a schedule.

01:09:51.953 --> 01:09:55.010
- I'm gonna take a step.
- I'll make my own events.

01:09:55.010 --> 01:09:58.528
- I'll be like, now, all
I want to do is work,

01:09:58.528 --> 01:10:00.558
but I'll schedule something
in like two weeks.

01:10:00.558 --> 01:10:02.213
'Cause it's not right
now, it's not right now,

01:10:02.213 --> 01:10:03.046
it's not work right now.

01:10:03.046 --> 01:10:04.627
Then it comes around and I'm
like, "Fuck I want to work."

01:10:04.627 --> 01:10:07.089
But I'm glad I scheduled
that because now can actually

01:10:07.089 --> 01:10:09.353
force myself to go and have a good time,

01:10:09.353 --> 01:10:11.199
and not think about doing work.

01:10:11.199 --> 01:10:12.642
- I feel like moving
has helped you as well

01:10:12.642 --> 01:10:14.942
'cause I remember before,
you never invite people

01:10:14.942 --> 01:10:15.895
to your place at all because-

01:10:15.895 --> 01:10:18.021
- It was a mess.
- It was a mess.

01:10:18.021 --> 01:10:19.959
- Well, Pewdiepie roasted me.

01:10:19.959 --> 01:10:22.363
(Mori and Garnt laughs)

01:10:22.363 --> 01:10:23.196
- It was terrible and it was also too far.

01:10:23.196 --> 01:10:24.130
- But now you're in a more central place,

01:10:24.130 --> 01:10:26.374
so it's easier to just invite people,

01:10:26.374 --> 01:10:27.734
and sort out your own place.

01:10:27.734 --> 01:10:28.956
- Because when I lived an hour away,

01:10:28.956 --> 01:10:31.680
like a minimum of an hour journey.

01:10:31.680 --> 01:10:34.240
An hour is a long time to lose in a day

01:10:34.240 --> 01:10:37.354
when I try and make every
God damn hour count.

01:10:37.354 --> 01:10:39.697
So when two hours, 'cause
there and back, right?

01:10:39.697 --> 01:10:41.078
now it's a lot quicker for me,

01:10:41.078 --> 01:10:43.598
which is great for most places.

01:10:43.598 --> 01:10:46.639
But yeah, I would spend
so much time traveling,

01:10:46.639 --> 01:10:49.757
and I'm not the kind of person
who can work on a train.

01:10:49.757 --> 01:10:50.796
I don't know about you.

01:10:50.796 --> 01:10:53.176
- Yeah, definitely not Tokyo trains.

01:10:53.176 --> 01:10:55.196
Yeah, If I'm standing,

01:10:55.196 --> 01:10:56.658
there's absolutely no
way I can do any work.

01:10:56.658 --> 01:10:57.696
And then sometimes-

01:10:57.696 --> 01:10:58.679
- I can, I figured out a way.

01:10:58.679 --> 01:11:00.540
Do you get this thing though, sometimes?

01:11:00.540 --> 01:11:01.373
- How, how?

01:11:01.373 --> 01:11:02.206
What work do you do on a train?

01:11:02.206 --> 01:11:03.328
(Mori chuckles)

01:11:03.328 --> 01:11:04.670
- Well, I can answer emails,
I can work on scripts

01:11:04.670 --> 01:11:06.376
'cause you can do it all on the phone.

01:11:06.376 --> 01:11:08.518
- Fuck off, can you work on
scripts on the train, Joey.

01:11:08.518 --> 01:11:12.308
(Mori and Garnt laughs)

01:11:12.308 --> 01:11:13.609
- Do you ever have, I don't know if this

01:11:13.609 --> 01:11:15.595
is another thing or this
is just a me thing, right?

01:11:15.595 --> 01:11:17.371
I have these things, right, it's an email,

01:11:17.371 --> 01:11:19.707
but it's an email that I
need to sit down and look at.

01:11:19.707 --> 01:11:22.648
It's a focus email, I can't
do it when I'm standing.

01:11:22.648 --> 01:11:26.171
I got to sit down and
be like, "Okay, okay."

01:11:26.171 --> 01:11:27.004
- [Mori] 100%.

01:11:27.004 --> 01:11:27.837
- Yeah, I don't have that (chuckles).

01:11:27.837 --> 01:11:28.670
- You don't?

01:11:28.670 --> 01:11:29.503
I'm envious of you.

01:11:29.503 --> 01:11:30.336
- I have that.

01:11:30.336 --> 01:11:32.312
I can't answer important
emails on my phone,

01:11:32.312 --> 01:11:34.775
I need to sit down on
a laptop or a computer

01:11:34.775 --> 01:11:35.794
or something.

01:11:35.794 --> 01:11:36.637
- It feels so much nicer.

01:11:36.637 --> 01:11:37.470
- [Garnt] Yeah, yeah.

01:11:37.470 --> 01:11:38.303
- A computer, have the big screen,

01:11:38.303 --> 01:11:40.080
so I can think about my
words on a bigger resolution.

01:11:40.080 --> 01:11:41.322
I don't know why that matters.

01:11:41.322 --> 01:11:43.717
- Do you activate different
neurons when you sit down?

01:11:43.717 --> 01:11:45.572
- Calli back me up here.

01:11:45.572 --> 01:11:46.596
Do you do this?

01:11:46.596 --> 01:11:47.730
- I mean, I agree, actually, entirely,

01:11:47.730 --> 01:11:48.972
especially when it comes to music.

01:11:48.972 --> 01:11:52.931
Though, sometimes I'll be
on a plane, on a train,

01:11:52.931 --> 01:11:54.672
I get my phone out, I'm
like, "I'm ready to work."

01:11:54.672 --> 01:11:56.536
And I'm like, "Nope, time for a nap."

01:11:56.536 --> 01:11:57.369
And I just put my phone away-

01:11:57.369 --> 01:11:58.202
- People who work on planes are like,

01:11:58.202 --> 01:12:00.646
just what happened in their childhood?

01:12:00.646 --> 01:12:01.479
(Mori laughs)

01:12:01.479 --> 01:12:02.312
- Oh no, I can work on planes.

01:12:02.312 --> 01:12:03.235
- What happened in your childhood?

01:12:03.235 --> 01:12:04.068
- I can work on planes.

01:12:04.068 --> 01:12:04.901
- That's fucked up.

01:12:04.901 --> 01:12:05.734
- Oh my God, how?

01:12:05.734 --> 01:12:06.567
- Working on a plane is different

01:12:06.567 --> 01:12:07.931
than working on a train, okay.

01:12:07.931 --> 01:12:08.764
- No, man.

01:12:08.764 --> 01:12:09.690
You work on a plane?
- With a train-

01:12:09.690 --> 01:12:10.523
- Yeah.

01:12:10.523 --> 01:12:11.356
(Garnt laughs)

01:12:11.356 --> 01:12:12.412
- Oh my God.

01:12:12.412 --> 01:12:13.650
- [Mori] Oh my God.

01:12:13.650 --> 01:12:14.483
- You're like this in the fucking cabin,

01:12:14.483 --> 01:12:16.632
there's people next to you,
they bring the food over,

01:12:16.632 --> 01:12:18.191
you're like, "Oh shit,
the fucking laptop."

01:12:18.191 --> 01:12:20.054
'Cause on a plane, you are-

01:12:20.054 --> 01:12:21.061
- I do it on my phone.

01:12:21.061 --> 01:12:22.054
- No.

01:12:22.054 --> 01:12:23.755
- No, no, you don't work
on your phone, Joey.

01:12:23.755 --> 01:12:24.588
(Mori and Chad laughs)

01:12:24.588 --> 01:12:26.048
You need a fucking laptop

01:12:26.048 --> 01:12:28.917
or at least a tablet, a phone?

01:12:28.917 --> 01:12:29.953
- That's pretty rough.

01:12:29.953 --> 01:12:31.779
- You can't work on a plane right?

01:12:31.779 --> 01:12:33.774
- No, I mean, what happens
is, I think I'm going to,

01:12:33.774 --> 01:12:34.607
so I bring my laptop.

01:12:34.607 --> 01:12:35.440
- The three levels of psychopaths.

01:12:35.440 --> 01:12:37.613
- I bring it in the carry on
and I put it on the table,

01:12:37.613 --> 01:12:38.838
and I'm ready to work.

01:12:38.838 --> 01:12:41.233
And then suddenly someone
