01:56:55.720 --> 01:56:57.386
because we kind of in the same thing,

01:56:57.386 --> 01:57:00.323
but we're all like our own unique kind

01:57:00.323 --> 01:57:01.156
of channel and whatnot.

01:57:01.156 --> 01:57:02.744
Is there ever like a frustrating thing

01:57:02.744 --> 01:57:04.584
'cause you obviously all the Vtube

01:57:04.584 --> 01:57:05.884
has come in as one package,

01:57:05.884 --> 01:57:08.125
it's like, this is the generation.

01:57:08.125 --> 01:57:09.164
How do you make sure

01:57:09.164 --> 01:57:10.481
that there's not this kind of weird sense

01:57:10.481 --> 01:57:12.966
of competition amongst fellow VTubers?

01:57:12.966 --> 01:57:14.661
Cause you're all kind of the same thing.

01:57:14.661 --> 01:57:16.444
I mean, you're not the same,

01:57:16.444 --> 01:57:19.996
but you're the same
target audience, right?

01:57:19.996 --> 01:57:22.858
Joey talks about manga anime

01:57:22.858 --> 01:57:24.797
and I might go and do something silly,

01:57:24.797 --> 01:57:27.857
gone so my fate, it's
totally different audience,

01:57:27.857 --> 01:57:30.405
even though we all kind of
in the same market, right?

01:57:30.405 --> 01:57:31.464
- [Garnt] Yeah, yeah.

01:57:31.464 --> 01:57:32.297
- With VTubing, I always wonder

01:57:32.297 --> 01:57:33.835
how do you like stop that from happening

01:57:33.835 --> 01:57:35.896
like a competition like that?

01:57:35.896 --> 01:57:37.879
- It's hard for me to speak on behalf

01:57:37.879 --> 01:57:39.409
of the entire VTuber community.

01:57:39.409 --> 01:57:40.242
- Yeah, yeah.

01:57:40.242 --> 01:57:42.210
- As much as I support
and love, like the work

01:57:42.210 --> 01:57:43.628
of what Indies are doing,

01:57:43.628 --> 01:57:45.846
I don't have enough energy in my life

01:57:45.846 --> 01:57:48.772
to go socialize with many outside of holo,

01:57:48.772 --> 01:57:50.908
which I think is a shame
and I wish I could,

01:57:50.908 --> 01:57:52.881
but it's kind of difficult to do.

01:57:52.881 --> 01:57:55.662
So I can really only speak about
what I've seen within holo,

01:57:55.662 --> 01:57:58.640
but I just feel like somehow

01:57:58.640 --> 01:58:01.638
there was some kind of magic involved

01:58:01.638 --> 01:58:02.924
in the selection process

01:58:02.924 --> 01:58:04.841
where they chose people

01:58:06.001 --> 01:58:10.834
that we just don't really get
extra jealous of each other.

01:58:11.684 --> 01:58:14.720
I mean, at least this is me
saying, from my perspective,

01:58:14.720 --> 01:58:16.280
I don't know what's going
through the other side.

01:58:16.280 --> 01:58:18.863
(all laughing)

01:58:20.726 --> 01:58:21.748
I can't speak on their behalf,

01:58:21.748 --> 01:58:24.854
but I can say for me genuinely,
the people that they chose,

01:58:24.854 --> 01:58:26.752
I look at them and I just
want to see them succeed.

01:58:26.752 --> 01:58:29.916
And I feel like part of me is questioning

01:58:29.916 --> 01:58:31.390
like, well, shouldn't you be wanting

01:58:31.390 --> 01:58:33.433
to be better than X and so-and-so,

01:58:33.433 --> 01:58:35.250
but I just can't parse that feeling.

01:58:35.250 --> 01:58:36.870
I just don't feel it, that is the truth.

01:58:36.870 --> 01:58:39.171
I mean, of course there's
me wanting to be my best,

01:58:39.171 --> 01:58:42.054
but I guess here's a good example

01:58:42.054 --> 01:58:43.070
I can give you from my past.

01:58:43.070 --> 01:58:46.553
My first really, really close friend ever

01:58:46.553 --> 01:58:48.555
was a friend that I met in middle school,

01:58:48.555 --> 01:58:49.671
who was the new kid.

01:58:49.671 --> 01:58:50.912
She moved to my city.

01:58:50.912 --> 01:58:52.710
I had no friends in that school.

01:58:52.710 --> 01:58:55.550
It was not great, but this new kid came

01:58:55.550 --> 01:58:58.451
and she was drawing, she
had how to draw manga book.

01:58:58.451 --> 01:58:59.530
- Hell yeah.

01:58:59.530 --> 01:59:02.813
- And I had been trying
to figure out like,

01:59:02.813 --> 01:59:04.148
what is that art style called?

01:59:04.148 --> 01:59:06.110
Because I didn't know
where to search for it.

01:59:06.110 --> 01:59:07.172
I was young, I had no idea.

01:59:07.172 --> 01:59:08.531
And so she explained it to me.

01:59:08.531 --> 01:59:09.889
She opened up the whole world to me

01:59:09.889 --> 01:59:10.974
and she let me borrow it.

01:59:10.974 --> 01:59:12.310
And that was when I started drawing.

01:59:12.310 --> 01:59:14.736
And I came to school the next day

01:59:14.736 --> 01:59:15.973
and people were like, wow,

01:59:15.973 --> 01:59:19.253
you can draw really well,
you both are really good.

01:59:19.253 --> 01:59:21.273
Some people were saying, Calli,

01:59:21.273 --> 01:59:23.690
you're maybe a little better.

01:59:25.659 --> 01:59:26.779
And I was like, no, that's not true.

01:59:26.779 --> 01:59:28.616
But that was the feeling that I got

01:59:28.616 --> 01:59:32.116
of, I can do something, and be good at it.

01:59:33.817 --> 01:59:35.220
And people are looking at what I'm doing

01:59:35.220 --> 01:59:38.953
and then of course my friend
was also like, oh, hell yeah,

01:59:38.953 --> 01:59:40.195
let's learn together.

01:59:40.195 --> 01:59:43.403
And we became friendly
rivals in that, like,

01:59:43.403 --> 01:59:46.224
we were always kind of working
alongside each other drawing.

01:59:46.224 --> 01:59:48.681
And like, maybe you show
your friend a picture,

01:59:48.681 --> 01:59:50.125
you drew, Hey, this is
my original character.

01:59:50.125 --> 01:59:50.958
Oh, cool, here's mine.

01:59:50.958 --> 01:59:51.884
And like, you're still friends,

01:59:51.884 --> 01:59:53.707
but there's this feeling of,

01:59:53.707 --> 01:59:56.034
I got to keep up with this person.

01:59:56.034 --> 01:59:58.402
And as I started being involved
in more art communities,

01:59:58.402 --> 02:00:01.520
as I grew older and met friends
on the internet, et cetera,

02:00:01.520 --> 02:00:04.004
we all were still cool and
friends with each other,

02:00:04.004 --> 02:00:07.261
but seeing other's hard work made us want

02:00:07.261 --> 02:00:09.322
to keep up that kind of thing.

02:00:09.322 --> 02:00:10.221
So-and-so drew this wall.

02:00:10.221 --> 02:00:11.284
I want to try doing that.

02:00:11.284 --> 02:00:12.817
Let me see how I can do.

02:00:12.817 --> 02:00:15.765
So it's not like an outright
feeling of jealousy,

02:00:15.765 --> 02:00:17.402
but it's a feeling of wanting to like,

02:00:17.402 --> 02:00:20.359
make yourself better to keep up, I guess.

02:00:20.359 --> 02:00:21.663
And it's like friendly competition, just-

02:00:21.663 --> 02:00:23.584
- That's good, it sounds very healthy.

02:00:23.584 --> 02:00:26.324
- Yeah. That's how it
was for me, personally.

02:00:26.324 --> 02:00:27.845
So no bad feelings.

02:00:27.845 --> 02:00:29.718
- That's a very good answer.

02:00:29.718 --> 02:00:30.800
(Garnt and Mori laughs)

02:00:30.800 --> 02:00:32.709
- That was most wholesome answer to all.

02:00:32.709 --> 02:00:33.725
- [Garnt] Yeah, yeah.

02:00:33.725 --> 02:00:35.768
- I was like, waiting for
the blood to be spilled.

02:00:35.768 --> 02:00:38.009
I'm kidding, I'm kidding.

02:00:38.009 --> 02:00:39.153
- And then I'd stabbed her with the pan.

02:00:39.153 --> 02:00:40.494
(all laughing)

02:00:40.494 --> 02:00:41.327
- [Mori] That's a habit-

02:00:41.327 --> 02:00:42.160
- Who's going now?

02:00:42.160 --> 02:00:42.993
(all laughing)

02:00:42.993 --> 02:00:43.826
- And a close group of friends

02:00:43.826 --> 02:00:46.631
that kind of like healthy
competition can form, I think

02:00:46.631 --> 02:00:49.595
instead of like a wide group
of people competing together,

02:00:49.595 --> 02:00:50.635
like a death game,

02:00:50.635 --> 02:00:53.676
for example, death games
on the mind, sorry guys.

02:00:53.676 --> 02:00:55.372
- I was going to say back
when the death games.

02:00:55.372 --> 02:00:57.496
- But if it's like a
small group of friends,

02:00:57.496 --> 02:01:01.397
it's really easy to foster,
like a healthy competition.

02:01:01.397 --> 02:01:02.395
- Yeah, yeah.

02:01:02.395 --> 02:01:03.228
- I think it's that whole mentality

02:01:03.228 --> 02:01:05.158
that a lot of people still struggle

02:01:05.158 --> 02:01:07.358
to understand of like,
if one person succeeds,

02:01:07.358 --> 02:01:09.941
then the rest can also come up.

02:01:11.456 --> 02:01:12.501
It's kind of mentality.

02:01:12.501 --> 02:01:13.761
And I feel that like
at least only YouTubers

02:01:13.761 --> 02:01:15.125
and stuff like that, and probably,

02:01:15.125 --> 02:01:16.478
in the VTuber community as well,

02:01:16.478 --> 02:01:17.500
where it's like,

02:01:17.500 --> 02:01:18.556
if one VTuber succeeds,

02:01:18.556 --> 02:01:19.995
then everyone in that same genre

02:01:19.995 --> 02:01:23.477
can also kind of rise up
together as a community.

02:01:23.477 --> 02:01:25.261
And I feel, especially

02:01:25.261 --> 02:01:26.700
like a lot of the smaller creators

02:01:26.700 --> 02:01:29.196
still don't quite understand that yet,

02:01:29.196 --> 02:01:30.514
I think in my eyes like where it's like,

02:01:30.514 --> 02:01:33.472
no, I need to be better than this person.

02:01:33.472 --> 02:01:34.926
- Normally the biggest channel

02:01:34.926 --> 02:01:39.459
that I needed genre is an
indication of the size.

02:01:39.459 --> 02:01:40.574
- The cap of the-

02:01:40.574 --> 02:01:41.723
- It's normally a good way.

02:01:41.723 --> 02:01:43.323
So if someone at the top is blowing up,

02:01:43.323 --> 02:01:44.568
that's normally a good thing.

02:01:44.568 --> 02:01:45.557
- [Garnt] Yeah exactly.

02:01:45.557 --> 02:01:46.390
- It's a trickle down.

02:01:46.390 --> 02:01:47.900
- Like I wouldn't have
come back to YouTube

02:01:47.900 --> 02:01:48.934
if I didn't see Joey blowing up

02:01:48.934 --> 02:01:50.721
'cause I thought when I quit YouTube,

02:01:50.721 --> 02:01:52.974
I'd like reach the ceiling.

02:01:52.974 --> 02:01:54.138
- I need my crown back.

02:01:54.138 --> 02:01:54.971
(all laughing)

02:01:54.971 --> 02:01:57.527
I was the Guinea pig.

02:01:57.527 --> 02:01:58.546
It's a metaphor.

02:01:58.546 --> 02:02:00.107
- 'Cause I was just like,

02:02:00.107 --> 02:02:02.372
I thought that I had reached the ceiling

02:02:02.372 --> 02:02:03.653
of anime content on YouTube

02:02:03.653 --> 02:02:04.609
and at the time I had,

02:02:04.609 --> 02:02:06.650
because anime just wasn't as popular.

02:02:06.650 --> 02:02:07.483
So I'm just like-

02:02:07.483 --> 02:02:08.316
- And then I was like Arrow boy.

02:02:08.316 --> 02:02:10.452
(all laughing)

02:02:10.452 --> 02:02:11.711
- I completed YouTube.

02:02:11.711 --> 02:02:14.294
(all laughing)

02:02:15.252 --> 02:02:18.137
- I came back for YouTube too (laughing).

02:02:18.137 --> 02:02:19.739
- The "Sequel" (laughing),

02:02:19.739 --> 02:02:20.792
long awaited "Sequel."

02:02:20.792 --> 02:02:23.072
You were saying, Calli?

02:02:23.072 --> 02:02:23.905
- No, you're good, you're good.

02:02:23.905 --> 02:02:25.394
I was thinking like personally,

02:02:25.394 --> 02:02:26.654
I think the most healthy way

02:02:26.654 --> 02:02:28.527
to like compete in general though,

02:02:28.527 --> 02:02:30.631
isn't to think about who
you're going to go past,

02:02:30.631 --> 02:02:32.796
but beating the you of yesterday.

02:02:32.796 --> 02:02:34.636
So inspirational hashtag.

02:02:34.636 --> 02:02:35.913
- Yeah, yeah.
- Pony tail.

02:02:35.913 --> 02:02:37.196
- [Connor] Just inspiration things.

02:02:37.196 --> 02:02:38.233
- - [Joey] Hash tag, motivated.

02:02:38.233 --> 02:02:39.628
- Sounds like I've seen now "Baki."

02:02:39.628 --> 02:02:41.271
(all laughing)

02:02:41.271 --> 02:02:44.615
- You're only as good as how
many times you've had sex.

02:02:44.615 --> 02:02:46.269
That's a "Baki."

02:02:46.269 --> 02:02:47.297
(all laughing)

02:02:47.297 --> 02:02:48.130
- That's right.

02:02:48.130 --> 02:02:49.411
But I mean, if you think about it though,

02:02:49.411 --> 02:02:50.518
there is some truth to it.

02:02:50.518 --> 02:02:53.496
As long as you are doing
better than your past self,

02:02:53.496 --> 02:02:56.178
as long as I'm doing better
than past me, I feel good.

02:02:56.178 --> 02:02:57.217
- Yeah.

02:02:57.217 --> 02:02:58.477
- Yeah. I mean, it's very
easy to compare yourself

02:02:58.477 --> 02:03:00.776
to others and then hold
yourself to some standards.

02:03:00.776 --> 02:03:03.243
You don't want to be the
gig of chat, but we count.

02:03:03.243 --> 02:03:04.741
- Yeah, would you have any advice

02:03:04.741 --> 02:03:06.639
to up-and-coming VTubers?

02:03:06.639 --> 02:03:09.825
Now they've had like a year of experience.

02:03:09.825 --> 02:03:11.364
- You're the senpai right now.

02:03:11.364 --> 02:03:13.864
- You're the senpai right now.

02:03:14.703 --> 02:03:16.368
- Let's see, maybe I'll pass along

02:03:16.368 --> 02:03:18.666
some advice that my
senpai had given to me,

02:03:18.666 --> 02:03:22.833
never stop doing new things,
keep trying new stuff

02:03:24.316 --> 02:03:26.598
and that's the only way to be, I think,

02:03:26.598 --> 02:03:28.618
is to keep pushing the boundaries

02:03:28.618 --> 02:03:31.776
and see what kind of wonderful
stuff can come from this.

02:03:31.776 --> 02:03:33.491
I think that's my advice to you guys,

02:03:33.491 --> 02:03:35.035
just passing on what I've been told.

02:03:35.035 --> 02:03:36.060
- Oh yeah.

02:03:36.060 --> 02:03:36.893
I mean, I'd say that's good advice

02:03:36.893 --> 02:03:39.124
for like any content
creators, VTuber or nodes.

02:03:39.124 --> 02:03:39.957
(screen whooshing)

02:03:39.957 --> 02:03:41.800
Do you feel sometimes that
you would have an easier time

02:03:41.800 --> 02:03:43.710
being like, say an indie VTuber,

02:03:43.710 --> 02:03:45.892
without having to like
worry about management

02:03:45.892 --> 02:03:46.725
and things like that?

02:03:46.725 --> 02:03:47.558
- That's right.

02:03:47.558 --> 02:03:50.235
Well, the way that I
kind of view it is yeah

02:03:50.235 --> 02:03:51.315
there are restrictions

02:03:51.315 --> 02:03:52.148
and for the most part,

02:03:52.148 --> 02:03:53.951
I get why they're in place.

02:03:53.951 --> 02:03:56.705
Right here, right now with me as I am,

02:03:56.705 --> 02:03:59.028
I'm happy to kind of
like work around things.

02:03:59.028 --> 02:04:01.730
For example, there are games
that I can always stream

02:04:01.730 --> 02:04:03.628
and I can't do it at all actually.

02:04:03.628 --> 02:04:04.669
And that's fine.

02:04:04.669 --> 02:04:06.225
A lot of them are ones that I like a lot,

02:04:06.225 --> 02:04:08.730
but at the end of the day, like I said,

02:04:08.730 --> 02:04:10.971
I've been trying to be
more positive recently.

02:04:10.971 --> 02:04:12.869
So the way that I think
about it is, you know what?

02:04:12.869 --> 02:04:15.231
Out of this list, I will
choose the ones that I like

02:04:15.231 --> 02:04:16.913
and I will have fun with them.

02:04:16.913 --> 02:04:19.949
And I think that's the
best way to go about it

02:04:19.949 --> 02:04:24.116
because you know, life is
long, for the most part-

02:04:26.744 --> 02:04:30.077
- Password? (laughing).

02:04:31.143 --> 02:04:35.711
- Because of me, it's not
as long as it could be.

02:04:35.711 --> 02:04:39.873
However, do a lot of things in your life

02:04:39.873 --> 02:04:42.277
and your existence.

02:04:42.277 --> 02:04:45.255
One life ends, one begins, et cetera

02:04:45.255 --> 02:04:47.439
that's how it was for me a long time ago.

02:04:47.439 --> 02:04:49.750
So you never know what
the future will hold.

02:04:49.750 --> 02:04:52.827
But right now with me
as I am, just the Mori

02:04:52.827 --> 02:04:53.855
in front of you,

02:04:53.855 --> 02:04:57.337
I can find workarounds
and ways to still have fun

02:04:57.337 --> 02:04:59.676
with the restrictions that are in place.

02:04:59.676 --> 02:05:02.376
And I think that that's kind
of the attitude to have,

02:05:02.376 --> 02:05:03.431
if you're going to go into this

02:05:03.431 --> 02:05:06.866
and join a big company, like hololive.

02:05:06.866 --> 02:05:08.949
You kind of work with it-

02:05:11.345 --> 02:05:12.362
- Is it something you were expecting

02:05:12.362 --> 02:05:15.629
the restrictions or was
this kind of a shock?

02:05:15.629 --> 02:05:16.668
- I think in the beginning

02:05:16.668 --> 02:05:20.127
I thought that it would
be a bit different.

02:05:20.127 --> 02:05:21.951
However, I don't think,
like I mentioned before,

02:05:21.951 --> 02:05:23.948
none of us knew how big
this was going to be.

02:05:23.948 --> 02:05:24.987
- Yeah.

02:05:24.987 --> 02:05:29.262
- And when that happens,
things kind of change a bit.

02:05:29.262 --> 02:05:30.590
- Right, when there's more money involved.

02:05:30.590 --> 02:05:31.769
- [Mori] Yeah.

02:05:31.769 --> 02:05:32.602
- More people get involved.

02:05:32.602 --> 02:05:34.868
- Imagine, just imagine.

02:05:34.868 --> 02:05:35.890
- To have a capitalism.

02:05:35.890 --> 02:05:36.906
- Business folks, man.

02:05:36.906 --> 02:05:38.003
(all laughing)

02:05:38.003 --> 02:05:39.170
- Things go rough.

02:05:39.170 --> 02:05:40.168
- [Connor] When stuff blows up,

02:05:40.168 --> 02:05:42.021
everyone wants to take credit for it.

02:05:42.021 --> 02:05:43.403
- That's how things are shawty.

02:05:43.403 --> 02:05:44.964
(all laughing)

02:05:44.964 --> 02:05:46.881
- We live in a society.

02:05:47.735 --> 02:05:49.112
- We (chuckles)-

02:05:49.112 --> 02:05:51.002
- Are trying to keep this politics free.

02:05:51.002 --> 02:05:52.098
Thank you very much.

02:05:52.098 --> 02:05:52.931
- [Connor] Society.

02:05:52.931 --> 02:05:53.841
- Yeah, society.

02:05:53.841 --> 02:05:55.762
- Just try and stay positive.

02:05:55.762 --> 02:05:57.718
- What are some of the top ideas

02:05:57.718 --> 02:05:59.483
that you would want to do

02:05:59.483 --> 02:06:01.527
if like, you have no restrictions at all?

02:06:01.527 --> 02:06:03.670
- Oh man, it's mostly games to be honest,

02:06:03.670 --> 02:06:05.996
that I think about collabs
that I'd want to do with people

02:06:05.996 --> 02:06:08.739
that just can't realistically happen.

02:06:08.739 --> 02:06:12.030
And it's like, there's
not just like protest

02:06:12.030 --> 02:06:15.095
from my side, either from management,

02:06:15.095 --> 02:06:16.994
but also from people
who watch me and like,

02:06:16.994 --> 02:06:18.874
I pay attention to that kind of stuff.

02:06:18.874 --> 02:06:20.877
They don't let it completely influence me,

02:06:20.877 --> 02:06:23.333
but like I do look at it and try

02:06:23.333 --> 02:06:25.295
to, factor in as much as I can see,

